{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791548454,"nonce":"iK8p9LIMSeTkaA70VwWGdob2SsI=","message":"Fixed in 781ebbb (Return deferred GC free pages when mutators become idle).\n\nSweep now tracks previously used blocks freed during busy periods, removes candidates on both small and large reuse paths, and drains surplus during a later quiet sweep. Virgin reservation pages and active TLAB blocks are excluded. Pending resident pages count toward idle collection eligibility even after an explicit major clears allocation pressure. Successful macOS REUSABLE/REUSE bookkeeping remains balanced, with 16 resident blocks (512 KiB) kept warm.\n\nMatched TreeMotion reusable-target replay at 840x840, application preset, 130 fixed-step frames and two explicit majors: before 171.94 / 175.78 MiB physical footprint, after 138.16 / 139.44 MiB. Mean reduction 35.06 MiB (~20%). Idle CPU was below 0.001% over the parked sample. All nine sampled RGBA frame hashes match. vmmap confirms the main heap mapping changes from roughly 52.4 MiB dirty to 16.8 MiB dirty, rather than merely lowering reported live allocation totals.\n\nInteraction after page return was also exercised: two motion passes in the same process; all 18 before/after sampled frames match, and small/large reuse regression tests preserve live TLAB data. Diagnostics show 1,172 pending blocks before idle -\u003e 1,156 reusable and 15 pending after wake (one pending block was reacquired). The second pass reacquired pages correctly and drained another batch.\n\nValidation: 17 GC unit tests, including finalizer lifetime and exact-once execution; retained 64 MiB object graph under repeated allocation bursts; 4,000 abandoned file handles with descriptor limit 128; actual OSR retier transfer and checksum; Ashui full pixel suite all pass. With Cranelift pinned and workers disabled, three alternating burst timing pairs are noisy (~0.8-1.1s), with no repeatable throughput regression.\n\nArtifacts (local, ignored): .ashui/memory-comparison/idle-return-125611, idle-reuse-125855, idle-gates-125947, idle-burst-cl-130209, idle-retier-130003, idle-pixels.log. The initial native-library-only test was invalid for the after arm: its executable selected the sibling runtime in target/release, rather than the modified fixture copy. The corrected comparison rebuilt/staged that actual runtime; later experiments used identical executables in the fixture directory so both selected the intended frozen native library.\n\nThis fixes the deferred page-return defect; it does not claim that the overall process footprint has reached the halving target. Decoded code, live AIR, live GC objects, GPU resources and allocator fragmentation remain separate costs. The later malloc-zone throttle experiment returned zero bytes and was discarded.","files":null}]}